      "draft": true,
      "body": "Metadata Family adoption could accept measures outside the original candidate range, and metadata-only Plans did not show exact selected ticks. Every selected component now validates its explicit range, including metadata-only mode. Incomplete/malformed, noninteger/reversed and outside ranges fail closed. Plan displays exact measure/tick intervals; adoption stores optional ticks in the existing selection field without rewriting source candidates or metadata-only MIDI.\n\n## Final verification — 2026-10-03 JST\nExact product HEAD: `c6a73c24706e31a95120201f1b552dbca43f6312`\n\n- [AI Assistant UI / exact-HEAD Chrome 37091731706](https://github.com/puitoybox-cloud/nova-studio/actions/runs/37091731706): SUCCESS\n- [Scoped MIDI repair 37091731710](https://github.com/puitoybox-cloud/nova-studio/actions/runs/37091731710): SUCCESS\n- `node --test`: 1063/1063 PASS, FAIL 0, skipped 0, both locally on freshly fetched exact remote HEAD and in CI\n- all 127 tracked JavaScript `node --check`: PASS\n- `git diff --check` against #278 base and working tree: PASS\n- Google Chrome 154.0.8037.57: 1440 / 820 / 390 PASS\n- 14 captures per width / 42 total: console error 0, console warn 0, pageerror 0, external request 0\n- browser regression retains full Family and partial normal/rejection flows; adds metadata Melody, Section outside-range rejection, metadata Family outside-range rejection, exact metadata measure/tick Plan display and adoption persistence\n- Plan -> Preflight -> Cancel -> Plan -> Preflight -> Confirm -> Apply -> Undo -> Redo -> Save -> Reopen PASS\n- Node integration additionally verifies JSON export/import, Backup/Restore and old-project load/render write 0\n- 27 new core regressions reproduced failures before their respective corrections; 2 new UI rejection regressions pass\n- artifact `music-ai-assistant-ui-verification` (11262584562) contains screenshots and actual checked-out HEAD report\n\n## Independent checkpoints and scope\nNew branch `feature/music-ai-family-metadata-range-v1`, based on freshly fetched Draft #278 `0777660e8871830b0d167fd00cbc13ced150d1c4`. Checkpoints `a408a89`, `cd5877d`, `c6a73c2` saved with non-force ref advances. Main `552d56eafddfd192970c09f7d6278696cf8775c3` and all existing Open PR HEADs were checked again and remain unchanged. All 23 existing Drafts were mergeable with successful returned CI runs at start. Main pages deployment 35718789435 was successful.\n\nFresh HEAD/mergeability/CI audit is saved in `verification/music-ai-family-metadata-range-audit.json`; implementation, failure reproduction, verification and remaining acceptance are documented in `verification/music-ai-family-metadata-range.md`. Existing Family transaction/history/persistence foundation is reused.\n\n## Remaining acceptance\nPhysical Intel Mac/Chrome and M1 iPad/Safari: separate synthetic project, Section or Metadata only M1-1, check Plan exact ticks, Preflight -> Confirm -> Undo -> Redo -> Save -> Reopen. Select outside the generated candidate range and verify BLOCKED with no mutation. Verify playback and Keystation Mini 32 MK3 recording/playback after an ordinary MIDI partial Apply. Linux Chrome does not establish physical-device acceptance.\n\nSection/Arrangement/Lyrics remain adoption metadata rather than project-section/instrumental rendering. Continuation remains subject to the existing dependency/conflict rule; no new policy is inferred here.\n\nSynthetic deterministic local only. No existing-PR/main changes, real songs/backups, automatic migration/load-time writes, deleted functionality, Live Provider/External AI/API Key communication, Ready/Merge/Auto Merge or force push. Draft only.",
