      "body": "Partial Family Apply now lets the user select components and an exact measure range before Plan, Preflight and explicit Confirm. Chord/Bass uses the existing Bass materializer; Section/Arrangement/Lyrics record adoption metadata. Metadata-only mode records the chosen components without changing MIDI. Empty or invalid selections fail closed. Changing a selection invalidates the previous Plan/Preflight.\n\nDeclared dependencies must be explicitly selected in the same candidate family. Arrangement-only and Lyrics-only selections show their missing-dependency reasons and cannot Apply. Nothing is added implicitly; metadata-only mode can explicitly include dependencies without writing MIDI. Melody/Continuation conflicts stay blocked.\n\nAdoption now shares the existing Editor snapshot history. Both MIDI and candidate status/adopted arrays/workspace history restore in one Undo/Redo unit, including metadata-only transactions. Save rebasing retains the runtime workspace binding. An Undo during an in-flight metadata-only save stays pending instead of being overwritten by completion of the older save. No saved MIDI field or separate Undo system is added. Exact partial ranges and counts in Plan reuse the existing narrowing bridge.\n\n## Final verification — 2026-10-03 JST\nExact product HEAD: `0777660e8871830b0d167fd00cbc13ced150d1c4`\n\n- [AI Assistant UI / exact-head Chrome verification 37037679357](https://github.com/puitoybox-cloud/nova-studio/actions/runs/37037679357): SUCCESS\n- [Scoped MIDI repair 37037679365](https://github.com/puitoybox-cloud/nova-studio/actions/runs/37037679365): SUCCESS\n- [Cache consistency 37037679319](https://github.com/puitoybox-cloud/nova-studio/actions/runs/37037679319): SUCCESS\n- `node --test`: 1034/1034 PASS, FAIL 0, skipped 0 (local and exact remote-head CI)\n- all 127 JavaScript `node --check`: PASS\n- `git diff --check`: PASS; CI checks the diff against this PR's #277 base\n- real Google Chrome 154.0.8037.57: 1440 / 820 / 390 PASS\n- each width: Melody-only, Bass-only, Section metadata-only, Melody+Bass and Family metadata-only -> Preview -> selection -> Plan -> Preflight -> Cancel with zero mutation -> Plan -> Preflight -> Confirm -> Apply -> one Undo -> Redo -> Save -> Reopen PASS\n- each width: Arrangement-only and Lyrics-only dependency rejection with zero MIDI/workspace/history mutation PASS\n- console error/warning/pageerror captures: empty; external-request captures: empty across all 33 browser captures\n- artifact `music-ai-assistant-ui-verification` includes screenshots and a report carrying the actual checked-out HEAD\n- Node regressions additionally cover JSON export/import, Backup/Restore, old-project load/render write 0, final Editor commit rollback, prior/later normal MIDI history, empty/invalid selection, family mismatch, stale Project/Track/range/workspace, protected ranges, exact meter-change tick 1000, legacy lock plus additive partial unlock, unchanged lock metadata, and Undo during an in-flight metadata-only save\n\n## Scope and remaining acceptance\nIndependent branch `feature/music-ai-partial-family-history-v1`, stacked on Draft #277 `f7383c988f9d98f0854a652edeb9171d949a8fd2`. Main `552d56eafddfd192970c09f7d6278696cf8775c3` and PR #271–#277 were freshly fetched and remain unchanged. Checkpoints are saved on GitHub.\n\nPhysical Intel Mac/Chrome, M1 i…18091 tokens truncated…cript files: `node --check` PASS\n- `git diff --check` PASS\n- synthetic save/reopen, JSON, Backup/Restore and Undo/Redo coverage PASS\n\nBrowser behavior remains the verified #269 implementation because this foundation is not loaded by either HTML entry point.",
