      "draft": true,
      "body": "A meter changes inside a measure previously left the browser and internal Editor closures on scalar timing, and browser recording did not share the existing Tempo Map service. This coordinated unit activates exact A timing throughout those paths, retains legacy tick protection and additive partial releases, and rejects protected edits atomically, including nested commands and corrupt Undo context. A real browser test found and fixed a save triggered by load-time scroll initialization.\n\nIndependent Draft combining the immutable GitHub sources of #262–#268 for coordinated browser review. Main and the existing PRs were not modified. It reconstructs current public sources; it does not assume the earlier unpublished local prototype exists on GitHub. #268's commit guard is explicitly coordinated with the A browser implementation, retaining its 33 original regression tests unchanged. No automatic merge is claimed.\n\nSource heads rechecked 2026-10-02 JST:\n- main: 552d56eafddfd192970c09f7d6278696cf8775c3\n- #262: a857c27674d6949488ff8884948499966f9bca40\n- #263: 9c877b267a181b560332e07071b7f86539eb1cbf\n- #264: c052f1614155f8ccd8e84235d6218e81ccc53758\n- #265: 7d2f0f49cdbc56e57fab6cef9a64681cc6168c8c\n- #266: 0101b246e219e3307ef55836b372f36fa331fa48\n- #267: f06cf5ac29d2fa96857ce0dc623d6e1696f016a6\n- #268: 909f5c41ee96c051ae7f0b5f8d982ff1f4c441ee\n\nInitial verification on b6834030ba386508f2d8023a367ed8c5cf6d35ec, before the final narrow-layout review:\n- [Checkpoint workflow 36969808601 SUCCESS](https://github.com/puitoybox-cloud/nova-studio/actions/runs/36969808601): node --test 936/936 PASS, 0 FAIL/skipped; all 111 JS syntax and git diff --check PASS.\n- Real Google Chrome 154: 1440/820/390 PASS; console error/warn/pageerror 0, external requests 0, load-time writes 0. Screenshots inspected; final-run artifacts are byte-identical to the inspected images.\n- Actual standalone UI checks exact bar 2 [1000,1720), ruler position, protected DOM-dispatched move/resize, editable move, explicit save/reopen, mixed legacy/new/release protection and native IndexedDB roundtrip. Meter tick 1000 and tempo tick 777 retained.\n- Seven original immutable meter scenarios and seven coordinated-session invocations PASS: 4/4, 3/4, 6/8, boundary, mid-bar, multiple and denominator changes.\n- Synthetic/memory save/reopen, actual JSON export/import and Backup/Restore preserve mixed protection and input data. Fake IndexedDB cases also PASS.\n- Recording onset/release, held-note Stop, playhead/loop timing and the actual metronome closure tested against the existing Playback timing service.\n\nFresh unchanged main: 774 / 768 PASS / 6 FAIL. Unchanged #267: 806 / 800 PASS / identical 6 FAIL, new failures 0. Combined #262–#267: 874/874. #268 commit stage: 907/907. Final coordinated reconstruction: 936/936. Combined #262 already resolves the known cache/selection baseline failures; no tests were disabled. #267 CI 36880714212 remains SUCCESS and #267 remains Draft.\n\nCommit paths covered: move, resize, delete, add, recording add, paste, repair apply, candidate apply, timeline resize, measure/range lock, partial unlock, Undo/Redo. Exact A ruler/grid/snap/range/resize/candidates are coordinated internally. Dependency revision checks fail closed. Explicit note flags and legacy aliases are preserved. No saved-song migration, actual backup modification, Live Provider/External AI communication, Ready/Merge/Auto Merge or force push.\n\nFinal narrow-layout review resolves the previously crowded short-bar labels and compressed controls at 390px. Linux runner has no Japanese fonts. Physical Mac/iPad touch/pencil, real MIDI permissions/device recording, audible metronome and audio/MIDI latency still require hardware. PR262's Intel Mac Audio-to-MIDI helper checks remain separate. The browser harness dispatches DOM events; it does not claim physical gesture or audible verification.\n\nFull verification record: [verification/coordinated-resume-20261002.md](https://github.com/puitoybox-cloud/nova-studio/blob/feature/music-coordinated-a-browser-v1/verification/coordinated-resume-20261002.md). Machine-readable browser results: verification/coordinated-browser-report-20261002.json. Checkpoint branch retained for resuming work; this independent PR remains Draft.\n\nFinal follow-up verification: a fresh disposable worktree combined the exact #262–#268 source heads, including #268's original workflow and tests, with zero textual conflicts: node --test 907/907 PASS, 0 FAIL and git diff --check PASS. This verifies the source stage separately from the manually coordinated browser unit. All 10 PR-triggered workflows plus the exact-head checkpoint workflow completed SUCCESS (11/11), including Intel macOS Audio Helper and Swift/macOS/iPad-simulator builds. These CI builds do not replace physical-device verification.\n\n\nFinal review — 2026-10-02 JST\n\nFinal product HEAD: 98b7067bbdf0a967c6d4c69b9be8721d688e7e52. All 11 current PR-triggered workflows completed SUCCESS, including [exact-head full-suite + real Chrome verification 36973666369](https://github.com/puitoybox-cloud/nova-studio/actions/runs/36973666369), Intel Mac Audio Helper packaging and Swift macOS/iPad-simulator builds. The browser workflow now explicitly checks out the PR head SHA rather than its synthetic merge SHA.\n\nA fresh clean checkout repeated node --test: 936/936 PASS, 0 FAIL/skipped. All 111 tracked JavaScript files pass node --check; main-to-final git diff --check PASS. Fresh exact #262–#268 disposable integration: zero textual conflicts, 907/907 PASS. The only cross-PR changed-file overlap is #262/#268 music-studio-editor.js; #269 coordinates that code with exact A timing. #263–#267 source files are byte-identical in #269, and #268's 33 original tests are unchanged. These are overlapping implementation stages, not eight PRs to merge independently.\n\n390px fix: keep core part names 92px and Mute/Solo 28px on a horizontally scrolling strip; preserve history controls. Short bars show their number first, keeping exact hit areas, aria labels, source ticks and full tooltip. Wider labels remain on one line. Final 1440/820/390 screenshots downloaded and visually reviewed. Browser assertions verify no control overlap, retained widths, narrow horizontal scrolling and label placement. All three widths PASS; console error/warn/pageerror 0, external requests 0, load-time writes 0. Native IndexedDB roundtrip, explicit save/reopen, lock/releases, protected DOM move/resize and editable move PASS. Browser artifacts: [11212229452](https://github.com/puitoybox-cloud/nova-studio/actions/runs/36973666369/artifacts/11212229452).\n\nSeven immutable meter cases and seven createCoordinatedSession cases rerun PASS: 4/4, 3/4, 6/8, boundary, exact mid-bar, multiple and denominator changes. Legacy/new range locks, partial releases, JSON reopen and Undo/Redo preserve exact tick protection. Recording onset/release, held-note Stop, frozen Tempo Map and actual metronome closure timing regressions PASS. Main and #262–#268 heads were rechecked unchanged; all PRs remain Draft. No actual songs/backups or migration, external Provider/AI calls, Ready/Merge/Auto Merge or force push.\n\nRemaining limits are physical Mac/iPad input, Japanese glyph rendering, audible metronome and audio/MIDI latency, hardware MIDI permissions/connect/disconnect, and #262 Intel Mac real-model Audio-to-MIDI accuracy (previous device FAIL is not superseded). Work-side review and browser tests are complete. A #269-specific HTTPS iPad preview or signed device install target has not been established; published main must not be reported as testing this PR. Hardware checks should use an independently verified final-head environment and synthetic projects. No physical-device start request is made by this review.\n",
